Looks like the error happens due to dependency to `BidiModule` from `@angular/cdk` which already uses new scope API for injectables https://github.com/angular/material2/blob/df488b0c68847fdef4cd58b9b8dbd0e644cb9b16/src/cdk/bidi/dir-document-token.ts#L28-L36

So you can replace `MatSnackBarModule` with `BidiModule` in `AppModule` and `MatSnackBar` with `Directionality` and catch the same error.

Here's also reproduction without `@angular/material`:

**app.component.ts**

```
import { Component, inject, Inject, InjectionToken } from '@angular/core';
import { DOCUMENT } from '@angular/common';

export const DIR_DOCUMENT = new InjectionToken<Document>('doc', {
  providedIn: 'root',
  factory: DIR_DOCUMENT_FACTORY,
});

export function DIR_DOCUMENT_FACTORY(): Document {
  return inject(DOCUMENT);
}

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  template: 'root template',
})
export class AppComponent {
  constructor(@Inject(DIR_DOCUMENT) doc: Document) {
    console.log(doc);
  }
}
```
https://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-issue-repro2-82qyhc?file=src%2Fapp%2Fapp.component.ts

